  "notes": "Modified cash basis village; governmental = General, Street, Fire and Ambulance, Other Governmental funds (Total Governmental Funds column, trimmed p4-6); business-type = Water and Sewer (p7-8, Total column). Statement 'Total revenues' 791,540 includes a 150,000 grant that is missing as a line in the printed statement (Fire column lines add to 39,304 vs printed 189,304); added from budget schedule p9 (Grant proceeds 150,000, also capital grants on p2). Governmental roll: 338,254 + 791,540 - 982,290 + 51,100 = 198,604. Transfers in/out are fund-column sums (total column blank). Business-type: 601,566 + 163,383 - 125,130 = 639,819. Budget schedule p9 (All Funds) is the only budget schedule; its interest line 4,971 split 4,831 gov / 140 proprietary using p3 and p8. County treasurer schedule p10 is a separate pass-through schedule; transfers to Village Treasurer shown as other financing. No liabilities on net position statement (total_liabilities null). Read pages 1-10 of 10 County Treasurer schedule (p10) left out of detail: the same money is already in the p9 All Funds budget schedule (property and motor vehicle taxes), so recording both would double count.",
